From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] spl: getf() refuses a descriptor without a vnode

getf() hands back a descriptor whatever it is, and spl_vn_rdwr(), the
only way the macOS layer reads or writes one, VERIFYs that it has a
vnode. libzfs relays pipes through a FIFO (libzfs_macos_wrapfd()) on the
paths it knows, but not on all of them: zfs send -nvP to a pipe (the
OpenZFS test zfs_send_006_pos, P3-01 checkpoint 2) reached the VERIFY
and panicked the kernel, and any process can pass /dev/zfs an anonymous
pipe or a socket. getf() now returns NULL for a descriptor that isn't a
vnode, so zfs_file_get() and the ioctl fail with EBADF.

Rebase-risk: low
---
diff --git a/module/os/neodarwin/spl/spl-vnode.c b/module/os/neodarwin/spl/spl-vnode.c
--- a/module/os/neodarwin/spl/spl-vnode.c
+++ b/module/os/neodarwin/spl/spl-vnode.c
@@ -235,7 +235,19 @@
 		}
 #endif
 		file_drop(fd);
+	}
+#ifdef __NEODARWIN__
+	/*
+	 * spl_vn_rdwr() can only do I/O through a vnode: refuse a descriptor
+	 * that has none (an anonymous pipe or a socket, which libzfs's FIFO
+	 * relay doesn't wrap everywhere), so the ioctl fails with EBADF
+	 * instead of the VERIFY in spl_vn_rdwr() panicking the kernel.
+	 */
+	if (sfp->f_vnode == NULL) {
+		kmem_free(sfp, sizeof (*sfp));
+		return (NULL);
 	}
+#endif
 
 	mutex_enter(&spl_getf_lock);
 	list_insert_tail(&spl_getf_list, sfp);
